 "deviations": [
  "Significance: the file has no p-value, so all 4,141 rows are treated as significant for H4 (likely Kircher 2019's pre-filtered subset; unverified). Sensitivity at |effect| >= 0.5 and >= 1.0.",
  "H5: significant vs non-significant cannot be formed; replaced by AUROC for |effect| >= 0.5 vs < 0.5 plus Spearman of each score vs |effect|.",
  "H5 element-matched score uses promoter/enhancer classes recalled from Kircher 2019, not verified from the paper.",
  "Effect sign (positive = alt raises expression) inferred from the TERT C228T/C250T check, not from a data card.",
  "Bootstrap clusters = elements present in each subset (16 at most), so CIs are wide.",
  "Added comparators not in PLAN (descriptive): AlphaGenome AVI, VEP 116 consequences, SpliceAI MANE d500, PLAN annotation flag.",
  "H4 direction for REGULATORY_CHANGE-only calls (362/403) and the 1 conflict: the PLAN says 'loss vs gain of the element', but REGULATORY_CHANGE has direction 'any' in the rule file, so MAGI states no direction. The sign of the largest of the 4 promoter/enhancer deltas is an analyst convention (declared in h4_direction_mapping before the deltas were read). After the audit, four other conventions, including the plan-literal one (DESTRUCTION/GAIN calls only), were added as H4.SENSITIVITY_direction_convention.",
  "EXPLORATORY H4 additions (always-loss baseline, within-element permutation, P(neg|pred loss) - P(neg|pred gain), mixed-sign fraction, element-equal weighting, dropping near-null elements): added because a pass driven by the base rate of losses would otherwise go unnoticed.",
  "Bootstrap fix: clusters are the elements present in each subset (an earlier draft resampled from all 16 elements even when a subset had fewer). Resamples with one class only are skipped for AUROC and counted (n_resamples_dropped_one_class).",
  "EXPLORATORY H5 additions after the audit: within-element-rank pooled AUROC and mean per-element AUROC, because pooled AUROCs mix score scales across elements."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "Within-element permutation p-values treat variants as exchangeable; neighbouring variants share windows and have correlated deltas, so the p-values are probably too small.",
  "Promoter/enhancer element classes (H5 matched score, convention d) and cell types are recalled from Kircher 2019, not verified against the paper.",
  "Candidates: many top LDLR candidates have mixed_sign=True (opposite-sign deltas near a tie); the list is weak evidence of mechanism."
 ]
}
